# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the two values from your Supabase project.
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL      Project Settings -> Data API -> Project URL.
#                        Shape: https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
#                        <project-ref> is the id already in the dashboard address bar:
#                        supabase.com/dashboard/project/<project-ref>
#                        No trailing slash, no /rest/v1.
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY Project Settings -> API Keys. Either works:
#                        - "Legacy API keys" tab -> "anon" "public"  (long eyJ... JWT)
#                        - "API keys" tab        -> sb_publishable_...
#
# NEVER put a secret key here (sb_secret_... / service_role). Vite inlines every
# VITE_* variable into the browser bundle, and a secret key bypasses row level
# security. The anon / publishable key is public by design; the RLS policies in
# supabase/schema.sql are what protect the data.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
